    "The new ASE Espresso calculator API: write_inputfiles(self, atoms, properties) - it takes atoms and properties. The calculate method is the main entry point. The calculator writes input files internally when calculate() is called. I need to understand the full workflow: (1) create calculator with profile, (2) assign to atoms.calc, (3) call atoms.get_potential_energy() which triggers calculate() which writes input files and runs pw.x. The write_inputfiles method is called internally by calculate(). So I should NOT call write_inputfiles directly - I should just use the calculator normally via atoms.calc = calc; atoms.get_potential_energy(). Let me update the test script to use this workflow and verify it works.",
